  "evidence_summary": "Among structural BTC levels that reached the touch, the 2020\u20132024 historical BREAK_FIRST frequency was 40.1% on touch 1 (N=1905), 37.6% on touch 2 (N=1101) and 33.6% on touch 3+ (N=1185); the touch-1-standardized differences were -2.3 pp (95% -6.0..+1.5 pp) and -6.6 pp (95% -10.7..-2.2 pp).",
  "integration": {
    "candidate": true,
    "checks": {
      "abs_d3_at_least_scale_and_ci_excludes_0": true,
      "control_not_the_same_pattern": true,
      "d2_same_sign_as_d3": true,
      "touch3_family_share_within_cap": true,
      "week_clusters": true,
      "year_share_within_cap": true,
      "year_signs": true,
      "years_same_sign": 4,
      "years_with_both_arms": 5
    }
  },
  "limitations": "Touch 2 and touch 3+ exist only for levels that were retested, so the contrast is conditional on survival to that touch and is not a causal effect of the touch. Touches of the same level, and levels in the same week, are dependent; the interval resamples weeks and does not model a richer dependence. The same price path can host several structural levels; confluence merges those that share a zone, and the rest still share the week shock. A 5m bar that hits both barriers is dropped rather than ordered. The sample is one venue and one symbol, 2020\u20132024, on a surface already exposed for level research. The association can differ by family and by year. REJECT_FIRST stays near 50% across buckets while NEITHER rises from 9.6% to 17.1% as BREAK_FIRST falls, so the touch-3+ difference is fewer resolved breaks, not a higher rejection rate. 2023 crude \u03943 is about zero, and the support-side crude \u03943 is much smaller than the resistance-side one. The pseudo-level control moves the other way. A historical frequency in this cohort is not a current probability.",
